paquet:commande:C3B.summary:
I built work package C3B, the command-map card (« la fiche »). The new test file passes (19/19) and `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` is clean. The card is not on screen yet: C6 has to plug it into the screen and add its CSS.

What now exists:

- **`src/ui/command/panelCard.ts`**: the `CardPanel` class. It builds DOM only and never reads the game; the screen passes everything in and gets the player's choices back through callbacks. It matches C3's `CardPanelLike` interface in `tacticalScreen.ts` exactly; tsc confirms the test's `const like: CardPanelLike = panel` assignment. The header comment explains how it works and lists every data-id.
  - **Card (S1).** Header with the title, sub-line, notes, « ‹ 1 / 7 › » (previous / next place), tabs when several repères are stacked, and the sticky line (« Rue suivante (2 / 7) — … »). Lines numbered 1–6 with « ▶ » on the highlighted one, plus « 0 ⋯ Autres ordres ici… »; when opened, the card shows the « Autres » list numbered. Lines carry 🔒 with the missing steps in words, or ⚖ « avant la dernière sommation ».
  - **Qui block.** « Qui : <unit> — <what it is doing> » with « à pied · 180 m · ~2 min ». Clicking the name opens the list. Buttons « Autre unité U » and the T button named by scope (« Toute la compagnie », « Toute la section », « Tout le groupe »). « Personne : barrières seules » for closing a street to cars. When Qui is fixed, neither button appears and the name does not open the list.
  - **Bottom of the card.** The sentence « Ce qui va se passer : … » with the rule in orange; « Donner l'ordre ⏎ » / « ‹ Retour Échap »; the keyboard hint line only when the screen sends one.
  - **Explanations.** All lines show them on a tall PC window; only the highlighted line does when the window is low or on the phone.
  - **Phone layout.** 40 px rows; ✕ in the header; one bottom row with « Qui : MISTRAL 2 · ~2 min [▸] [Donner l'ordre] »; no sub-line or sentence (the §2.2 height budget).
  - **Qui list (S2).** « Qui envoyer ? » with numbered rows and « ✓ proposée » on the game's choice. A « Renforts des commissariats » header appears before station units. Clicking a row picks it. Tick boxes plus « Valider » pick several; ticks made with the pointer survive the screen's 10 Hz redraw, and ticks the screen sets with Espace replace them.
  - **Legal confirmation (S3).** The numbered steps ①②③ with « Faire les étapes dans l'ordre ⏎ ». For a ⚖ line: « L'ordre part avant la dernière sommation : vous en répondrez. » with « Donner l'ordre quand même ⏎ » and « Faire d'abord les sommations ». When the chain is impossible: the reason in one line and only « ‹ Retour ».
  - **Order given (S4).** A green « ✓ ORDRE DONNÉ — <text> » over the card, with « Annuler l'ordre X » while the order can still be cancelled.
  - **Input.** Mouse and trackpad: hovering a line previews it, leaving the card hands back to the keyboard line, a click sends. Touch: the first tap only highlights; a second tap on the same line, or « Donner l'ordre », sends. Opening a different card resets this, so a tap is never carried over to another card. When Safari's click does not say it was a touch, the type of the press is used. Every button has tabindex="-1", and pressing one does not take focus from the map.
  - **Pure helpers** for tests and integration: `cardView`, `whoView`, `whoRows`, `defaultExtra`, `distanceText`, `etaText`, `travelLine`, plus the exported label constants.
- **`src/ui/command/styleCard.ts`**: `CARD_CSS` (prefix « cc- »). Rows 52 px (40 px on the phone), buttons 44 px (48 px on touch). The highlight is not only colour: « ▶ » plus a thick yellow left border. It also styles S3, S4 and the Qui list, and the keyboard keys are hidden on touch devices.
- **`tests/unit/ui-command.fiche-dom.test.ts`**: two real headless games at the Concorde (a commandant and a chef de groupe). The cards come from `buildCard` and `intentCandidates`, the proposed unit from `proposeWho`, the sentence from `sentenceOf`, and the legal steps from `legalCheck`. They are rendered into a small fake DOM written inside the test file. It covers every test the plan lists for C3B, and also:
  - the « Autres » list;
  - a fixed Qui on a unit card;
  - the Qui list (one click, ticks then « Valider », ticks set by the screen);
  - the ⚖ variant of S3, and S4 with and without « Annuler l'ordre »;
  - the low-window rule;
  - 🔒 lines say what is missing in words;
  - focus is never taken and every listener is removed on `dispose()`;
  - the CSS sizes;
  - the type check against `CardPanelLike`.

