  - the back() order as a pure function;
  - sticky intentions B / S / I against E / N / D;
  - the 0.6 s Entrée guard;
  - the state transitions;
  - `unitsByRecentOrder`;
  - the legal chip texts (and that no digit is ever shown);
  - the read-only banner and framing;
  - one real headless session (commandant, Concorde, real streets): B then Entrée ×3 moves through four distinct real exit streets, `withVerbFirst` puts « Se replier ici » and « Barrer » among the six lines, the unit card fixes Qui, and « À traiter » holds at most 3 real repères.
- After updating them: `ui-command.barrage-passants`, `ui-command.barrages-nasse`, `ui-command.clavier`, `ui-command.suivre-libelles`, `ui-command.tactique-cadrage`, `ui.system`: 7 files / 65 tests passed (run together with carte-clavier).
