intégration:commande.summary:
I integrated the « commande » redesign. Packages C1 to C7 were already wired together and coherent:
- `setTacticalParts` is installed by `CommandSystem.init` (through `tacticalParts.ts`);
- the legal chain is ticked by `CommandSystem.update` with `ctx.clock.now`;
- per-session state is reset on `session:started` (`legalChain.reset`, nasse, issued orders);
- `MEMORY` / `ORDERED` are keyed per session;
- I found no `Math.random` / `Date.now` in the simulation path, and no TODOs.

What I completed or fixed on top of that:

1) The RESTART NOTE's liaison slot is now a working line. `crowd.core.setLiaison` exists in this tree. « Négocier un parcours (liaison) » is the first entry of « Autres ordres ici… » on the main cortège card. It shows only when:
   - the player commands the whole operation (level `tout`);
   - the crowd service has `setLiaison`;
   - the liaison team is not already in contact (the director's `liaison` flag).
   Sending it calls `setLiaison(true)`, says it on the radio (« LIAISON ICI MISTRAL… ») and moves no unit; the line then disappears. Code: `cardTypes.ts` (`liaison` action and the `CardEnv.liaison` field), `reperes.ts` (`liaisonState`), `intents.ts`, `sendLine.ts`, `preview.ts`. Covered by a unit test and a new browser scenario, `verif-commande-liaison.mjs` (9/0). The main repository's `crowd:liaison` event will fire on its own after the merge. « Rendre compte » on the radio screen is untouched (`radioScreen.ts` is not modified).

2) §7.1: the field situation panel no longer shows « licite 1 · autorisée 1 ». It uses the chip's words (« Mains nues », « Gaz »…). It adds « vous autorisez : … ⚠ » only when the authorisation is above what the law allows. I removed the dead `FORCE_LABELS` / `FORCE_SHORT` (with « GM2L ») from `orders.ts`.

3) After « Faire les étapes dans l'ordre », the card header said « ✓ ORDRE DONNÉ » although the order only leaves at the end of the chain. It now reads « ✓ ÉTAPES LANCÉES — <plan> », with a second line « l'ordre partira après la dernière étape ».

4) Phone card (844×390):
   - stacked place tabs now sit in the header row in place of the title;
   - the sheet now rises to the top of the screen; the top-bar buttons stay to its left;
   - compact header, list and footer padding are tighter.
   The six lines, « 0 Autres ordres ici… » and « Donner l'ordre » now fit without scrolling. Before, row 0 was cut, and with tabs lines 6 and 0 needed scrolling. The phone scenario now checks this.

5) The command map's radio subtitles showed the top of a clipped third line in their bottom padding. That padding is now a transparent border.

6) Field HUD at 1280×800: « Plus tard Maj+P » stuck out past the right edge of the adjoint's proposal card; the buttons now fit. At window heights below 760 px the one-line proposal showed only « L'adjoint propose : Te… ». It now reads « Adjoint : <title> » on up to 2 lines.

7) Two test fixes:
   - `ui-command.panneaux.test.ts` failed depending on machine load. The maps scene refreshes on the real-time clock, so a fast run read a stale unit order. The test now calls `scene.invalidate()` before re-reading the scene.
   - In `verif-fin-chef`, the place click could land on a crowd. `freeMapSpot` (`verif-fin-lib.mjs`) now also avoids crowds and incidents.

The `ui.hud-model` force-label assertion was updated, as §7.1 intends.

`tsc` is clean. Every targeted unit group passes. All browser scenarios that were run pass, except `verif-fin-chef` part E (run-over test, outside the command UI; part E was not re-run after the fixes).

